WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:02.935
-Well, a lot is going on

00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:04.704
in the world of
Trump-adjacent weirdos.

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:08.141
A judge has ruled that a series
of major defamation lawsuits

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:10.443
against three Trump allies
who lied about the election

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:13.146
can move forward.
A cyber expert admitted

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:15.948
that MyPillow CEO Mike Lindell
has no proof

00:00:15.948 --> 00:00:19.152
for his election lies.
And a damning new transcript

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:20.954
from a separate case
has emerged,

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:23.155
in which Rudy Giuliani
told federal agents

00:00:23.155 --> 00:00:25.325
it's okay to lie during
a political campaign.

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:27.626
For more on this, it is time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:27.626 --> 00:00:31.230
[ Theme music plays ]

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.833
The lie that Donald Trump
won the 2020 election

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:37.103
is the central animating belief
of Republican politics today.

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:39.071
That's why
GOP state legislatures

00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:41.774
in states like Georgia and Texas
have been racing

00:00:41.774 --> 00:00:43.643
to pass voter suppression laws

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:46.612
despite zero evidence
of any widespread fraud.

00:00:46.612 --> 00:00:48.481
In fact, according to Vox,
Georgia Republicans

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:50.183
are already putting
their new law to use.

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:51.484
I mean, damn, that was fast.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:53.186
The next election
is 15 months away,

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:55.154
and they're already
trying to undermine it.

00:00:55.154 --> 00:00:57.890
I never think that far ahead
about anything.

00:00:57.890 --> 00:00:59.258
Every single year,
I say to myself,

00:00:59.258 --> 00:01:00.793
"I'm going to get my wife
something great

00:01:00.793 --> 00:01:02.829
for our anniversary," and
the next time I think about it

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:04.397
is when my wife says,
"Happy anniversary."

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.765
And you know how they say,
"It's the thought that counts"?

00:01:06.765 --> 00:01:08.134
Well, it turns out,
that's bull [Bleep],

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:09.502
because I assure you,
I thought about it.

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:11.503
Like, I can show you
the reminder

00:01:11.503 --> 00:01:13.606
I wrote for myself
in my Notes app,

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:15.675
although the Notes app
is a trap.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:17.310
You only open it
to write stuff down.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.845
You never open it
to read anything.

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:20.947
It would be just as effective
to write your reminders

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:22.481
on a rock and
then drop it in a pond.

00:01:22.481 --> 00:01:24.784
Go ahead, open your Notes app
right now.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:26.018
I guarantee, all that's in there

00:01:26.018 --> 00:01:28.254
is a Wi-Fi password
to some Airbnb

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:29.656
and a phone number
you've never called.

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:32.758
Besides, my best gifts
are my impressions.

00:01:32.758 --> 00:01:34.627
Why waste money
on a physical present

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:36.929
which I can just give my wife
the joy and delight

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:38.130
of a Mike Lindell.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.799
[As Lindell]
Happy anniversary, honey.

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.867
I thought you'd enjoy
this impression

00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:45.205
more than some earrings
from De Beers [da Bears]!

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:48.641
Where you going?
I got more Bears fun for you.

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:52.712
Oh, God, no!
Oh, she's leavin' me!

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:56.515
Oh, no!
Here comes da tears!

00:01:56.515 --> 00:01:59.619
[ Normal voice ] By the way,
we focused a lot

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:02.155
on the voter suppression aspects
of these laws,

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:04.424
which are definitely bad,
but even worse,

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:06.325
these laws also
give Republicans the power

00:02:06.325 --> 00:02:08.328
to subvert election outcomes
they don't like.

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:11.063
For example, in Georgia,
"the most ominous provisions

00:02:11.063 --> 00:02:13.566
of this new law allow
the state election board,

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:15.101
which is dominated
by Republicans,

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:18.070
to seize control of
county election boards.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:19.705
Those boards
can disqualify voters,

00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:21.941
move polling precincts,
and potentially even refuse

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:23.442
to certify an election count."

00:02:23.442 --> 00:02:25.711
Well, thankfully, there's
no danger of that.

00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:28.281
I can't recall a time
when Republicans ever refused

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:29.648
to certify an election count.

00:02:29.648 --> 00:02:32.151
What's that? In January?
Well, I wasn't here.

00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:34.186
I was at impression camp,
remember?

00:02:34.186 --> 00:02:36.589
I came back, and you asked me
if I worked on my Liam Neeson,

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:38.290
and I said, "No,
only a very few people

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:39.792
can do Neeson,
because it requires

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:42.061
[As Neeson] a very particular
set of skills."

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:43.996
[ Normal voice ]
Misdirect. Classic.

00:02:43.996 --> 00:02:46.265
Anyway, remember
how Trump called

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:49.636
the Georgia secretary of state
and tried to badger him

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:52.171
into magically finding enough
votes to change the outcome?

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:54.140
Well, basically,
Republicans in Georgia

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.308
made it easier for him
to succeed next time

00:02:56.308 --> 00:02:58.277
by allowing Republicans
to take control

00:02:58.277 --> 00:03:00.646
of the county election board
in, say, Fulton.

00:03:00.646 --> 00:03:01.980
That where we're at right now.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.016
Republicans saw a guy
possibly commit a crime

00:03:04.016 --> 00:03:06.419
and decided to make it easier
for him to pull it off.

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:08.554
It's like if there was a rash
of car break-ins

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:11.557
in your neighborhood
and the town council responded

00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:14.660
by outlawing The Club.
It's a true story.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:17.529
Sal wrote that joke,
and Mel, who makes the graphics,

00:03:17.529 --> 00:03:19.866
is so young, she didn't know
what a Club was.

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:21.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.435
She thought it was a nightclub,

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:24.603
and the easy way for Mel
to remember, moving forward,

00:03:24.603 --> 00:03:26.705
is when Sal says "The Club,"
it's always

00:03:26.705 --> 00:03:28.040
the one you put on the car

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.510
and not the one that Sal is
too old to get into.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:31.811
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:33.846
"I'm the guy who writes
"A Closer Look'!"

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:36.315
"Just keep it movin', buddy."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:38.851
"I'm going to write a
'Closer Look' about this club."

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.253
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:42.621
And yet, even as Republican
voters and lawmakers

00:03:42.621 --> 00:03:43.923
continue to codify the lie

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:45.558
that the election
was stolen from Trump,

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:47.293
the people who push that lie
are facing

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:49.562
major legal and financial
consequences for it.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.297
On Wednesday, a judge ruled

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:53.265
that a series
of defamation lawsuits

00:03:53.265 --> 00:03:55.902
brought by the election
technology company Dominion

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:59.405
against three Trump-adjacent
crazy people can move forward.

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:02.608
-A federal judge will allow
three major defamation lawsuits

00:04:02.608 --> 00:04:05.544
to go forward against some of
former President Trump's

00:04:05.544 --> 00:04:08.414
most loyal supporters.
Rudy Giuliani, Sidney Powell,

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:11.450
and MyPillow CEO Mike Lindell
are all being sued

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.653
for billions of dollars
in damages

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:16.188
by Dominion Voting Systems,
which is the company

00:04:16.188 --> 00:04:18.523
that they falsely accused
of election fraud.

00:04:18.523 --> 00:04:19.792
-Dominion, which makes

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:22.061
voting machines
used in the 2020 election,

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:24.263
wants billions of dollars
in damages.

00:04:24.263 --> 00:04:27.934
The judge who issued the ruling
was appointed by Donald Trump.

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:30.369
-Okay, so, there are only
two plausible explanations

00:04:30.369 --> 00:04:32.571
for what happened here.
Either a federal judge

00:04:32.571 --> 00:04:35.474
appointed by Donald Trump
ruled that unfounded claims

00:04:35.474 --> 00:04:37.577
of election fraud
made by three Trump allies

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:40.046
were not exempt
from defamation loss

00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:43.115
or Hugo Chávez teamed up
with China and the CIA

00:04:43.115 --> 00:04:45.484
to use Italian military
satellites

00:04:45.484 --> 00:04:47.453
to hack the judge's computer
and alter his opinion,

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:48.887
which was then
printed out on paper

00:04:48.887 --> 00:04:51.024
smuggled in from China,
covered in bamboo fibers.

00:04:51.024 --> 00:04:52.524
The only way
we can know for sure is

00:04:52.524 --> 00:04:54.594
if we take the judge's ruling
to a cabin in Montana,

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:56.562
examine it under
a powerful ultraviolet light,

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:58.530
then bury it in the backyard,
wait three days,

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:00.032
and see if it rains.

00:05:00.032 --> 00:05:01.834
Man, I wish I could have seen
Rudy's face when he found out.

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.535
And that's saying something,
because I've never wished

00:05:03.535 --> 00:05:05.271
to see Rudy's face.

00:05:05.271 --> 00:05:06.773
I mean,
it could have been anything.

00:05:06.773 --> 00:05:08.407
The man has a whole
range of expressions.

00:05:08.407 --> 00:05:12.678
Maybe it was this... or this...
or this...or this.

00:05:12.678 --> 00:05:13.980
Who knows?

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.348
He's the man
of a thousand faces.

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:17.383
And I'm guessing,
when Lindell found out,

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:19.685
he was so shocked,
his mustache fell off.

00:05:19.685 --> 00:05:22.755
Why does Lindell's facial hair
look so cartoonishly fake?

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:24.290
He looks like a gambler

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:26.625
who changed his look
to hide from the mob.

00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:28.461
He wants to see
everyone else's voter I.D.,

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:30.829
but there's a good chance, if
we saw his driver's license,

00:05:30.829 --> 00:05:32.231
it would look like this.

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:35.067
Now, Lindell has been at
a so-called Cyber Symposium

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:38.037
in South Dakota this week,
continuing to spread the lie

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:39.171
that the election was rigged,

00:05:39.171 --> 00:05:40.940
and he's been livestreaming
the whole thing.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:44.277
So we got to see him react
to this ruling in real time.

00:05:44.277 --> 00:05:45.644
And as you may have guessed,

00:05:45.644 --> 00:05:47.980
he showed his trademark
calm and restraint.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.182
-Oh, okay.
This, I found out.

00:05:50.182 --> 00:05:54.020
I do want to say this
before they come out.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:57.256
Okay, remember
I told you that, um...

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:59.091
[ Audience murmurs ]

00:05:59.091 --> 00:06:02.728
This is -- This is news to me.
I read this for the first time.

00:06:02.728 --> 00:06:06.098
This is really bad
for our country, everybody.

00:06:06.098 --> 00:06:09.235
They -- Everybody needs to
really listen up.

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:11.537
This is just new to me.

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:15.208
"The federal judge
just put in, this afternoon,

00:06:15.208 --> 00:06:17.844
Dominion Voting Systems
can move forward

00:06:17.844 --> 00:06:21.247
with defamation lawsuits
against Rudy Giuliani,

00:06:21.247 --> 00:06:24.416
Sidney Powell,
MyPillow CEO Mike Lindell."

00:06:24.416 --> 00:06:25.851
-Are you just reading this
for the first time?

00:06:25.851 --> 00:06:28.287
-I'm just reading it.
Can you believe that?

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:31.324
-[ Shouting indistinctly ]
-That is horrible, everybody.

00:06:31.324 --> 00:06:33.793
Your First Amendment rights
to free speech

00:06:33.793 --> 00:06:36.329
just got blown out of the water.
It's over.

00:06:36.329 --> 00:06:38.564
You can get sued
for everything now.

00:06:38.564 --> 00:06:40.499
Nothing matters anymore.

00:06:40.499 --> 00:06:43.235
-Watching someone get bad news
in real time,

00:06:43.235 --> 00:06:45.638
at their own symposium,
is my new kink.

00:06:45.638 --> 00:06:48.541
This is like
if Tony Robbins lost it

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:50.175
during one of
his self-help seminars.

00:06:50.175 --> 00:06:52.345
[As Robbins] You have to
push out your negative feelings

00:06:52.345 --> 00:06:53.880
and take control
of your emotions.

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:55.113
Hold on. It's my assistant.

00:06:55.113 --> 00:06:56.883
What do you mean
they don't have blue jeans?!

00:06:56.883 --> 00:07:01.053
What kind of self-respecting
sale runs out of blue jeans?!

00:07:01.053 --> 00:07:04.590
I will not call Don Pablo!
My whole day is ruined now!

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.358
[ Normal voice ] That's why
I like how Lindell

00:07:06.358 --> 00:07:07.860
suddenly takes on
the exhausted energy

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.962
of a substitute teacher when
he's trying to tell everyone

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:11.130
how much deep [Bleep] he's in.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.965
[As Lindell] Hey, guys.
Listen up, please.

00:07:12.965 --> 00:07:15.067
Uh, come on, guys.
If we don't do the lesson plan,

00:07:15.067 --> 00:07:16.769
we can't watch "Free Willy"
on laser disk.

00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:18.637
Hey, come on.
What are you doing on the couch?

00:07:18.637 --> 00:07:20.406
Come on, guys,
you can't type "boobs," okay?

00:07:20.406 --> 00:07:23.075
And don't tell me the calculator
was hacked by Hugo Chávez.

00:07:23.075 --> 00:07:25.777
Why? Because you're gonna get
sued by Texas Instruments.

00:07:25.777 --> 00:07:27.780
[ Normal voice ] The best part
of that clip, though,

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:29.749
is how Lindell involves
everybody else in the room

00:07:29.749 --> 00:07:31.350
by telling them
their free speech rights

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:32.718
are blown out of the water.

00:07:32.718 --> 00:07:35.354
Like whatever happens to him
is happening to America.

00:07:35.354 --> 00:07:37.823
[As Lindell] Guys, bad news,
the doctor called,

00:07:37.823 --> 00:07:40.559
and it looks like America
has super-high cholesterol.

00:07:40.559 --> 00:07:43.596
No more lunch ribs for America.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:43.596 --> 00:07:45.297
[ Normal voice ] By the way,

00:07:45.297 --> 00:07:47.499
as the symposium
has been happening,

00:07:47.499 --> 00:07:50.836
a cyber expert who has examined
Lindell's supposed evidence

00:07:50.836 --> 00:07:52.638
apparently admitted
they can't actually prove

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:54.005
any of his claims.

00:07:54.005 --> 00:07:56.942
It's also very complicated
and also extremely insane.

00:07:56.942 --> 00:07:59.345
But to boil it down for you,
"The Washington Times" reported

00:07:59.345 --> 00:08:01.647
that "the key data
underpinning the theory

00:08:01.647 --> 00:08:03.448
that China hacked
the 2020 election

00:08:03.448 --> 00:08:06.152
unveiled at the Cyber Symposium
is illegitimate."

00:08:06.152 --> 00:08:08.720
The cyber expert said,
"We were handed a turd."

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:12.592
Yes, but in fairness that's
what they use to fill MyPillows.

00:08:12.592 --> 00:08:15.795
Rock-hard, calcified turds.

00:08:15.795 --> 00:08:18.464
Honestly, poor cyber experts.
You go to school

00:08:18.464 --> 00:08:20.399
to get a degree
in computer science,

00:08:20.399 --> 00:08:21.667
spend your whole career
mastering

00:08:21.667 --> 00:08:23.835
a highly specialized skill
that would be

00:08:23.835 --> 00:08:26.472
actually very helpful in today's
high-tech economy,

00:08:26.472 --> 00:08:29.575
and then a psycho pillow magnate
hands you what I'm guessing is

00:08:29.575 --> 00:08:31.677
a garbage bag full of
dry-cleaning slips

00:08:31.677 --> 00:08:33.245
and CVS receipts
and said,

00:08:33.245 --> 00:08:35.714
[As Lindell] I need you to
switch who the president is.

00:08:35.714 --> 00:08:37.616
[ Normal voice ] So,
Trump's gang of weirdos

00:08:37.616 --> 00:08:39.518
has these
big defamation lawsuits

00:08:39.518 --> 00:08:42.320
hanging over their heads.
And exactly -- I'm guessing

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:45.992
it's not exactly going to help
Rudy Giuliani in 2018,

00:08:45.992 --> 00:08:47.726
according to a
newly released transcript

00:08:47.726 --> 00:08:49.095
from an interview
with federal agents.

00:08:49.095 --> 00:08:51.564
He basically admitted
that he thinks it's okay

00:08:51.564 --> 00:08:53.533
to lie during
a political campaign.

00:08:53.533 --> 00:08:55.601
-"The Washington Post"
now reporting

00:08:55.601 --> 00:08:57.703
that ex-Trump attorney
Rudy Giuliani,

00:08:57.703 --> 00:09:00.272
who took Trump's election fraud
claims to court

00:09:00.272 --> 00:09:02.708
and failed
told federal agents

00:09:02.708 --> 00:09:04.777
back in 2018
it was okay

00:09:04.777 --> 00:09:08.080
to "throw a fake"
in the course of a campaign.

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:10.282
"The Post" says
that during that same interview,

00:09:10.282 --> 00:09:13.986
Giuliani's then-law partner
Marc Mukasey added

00:09:13.986 --> 00:09:15.654
that during a campaign,

00:09:15.654 --> 00:09:19.024
"you're under no obligation
to tell the truth."

00:09:19.024 --> 00:09:21.160
-That's right,
Rudy told federal agents

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:24.563
it was okay to "throw a fake"
during a political campaign.

00:09:24.563 --> 00:09:27.266
First of all, why did he use
the term "throw a fake?"

00:09:27.266 --> 00:09:28.801
Was he watching a boxing match

00:09:28.801 --> 00:09:30.836
in the back of
a Staten Island butcher shop?

00:09:30.836 --> 00:09:32.437
[As Giuliani] I paid him
100 bucks to throw a fake.

00:09:32.437 --> 00:09:34.640
I told him to make one hit
and then make this face.

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:35.908
[ Normal voice ]
But the funniest --

00:09:35.908 --> 00:09:37.309
can't believe
we had another one.

00:09:37.309 --> 00:09:39.044
But the funniest part about this
admission from Rudy, though,

00:09:39.044 --> 00:09:41.213
is that it was seemingly
totally unnecessary.

00:09:41.213 --> 00:09:43.716
His law partner at the time,
a guy named Marc Mukasey,

00:09:43.716 --> 00:09:45.817
was trying to gently explain
that sometimes,

00:09:45.817 --> 00:09:48.253
people in general exaggerate
in political campaigns.

00:09:48.253 --> 00:09:49.888
Not Rudy specifically.

00:09:49.888 --> 00:09:52.257
But Rudy couldn't help
but chime in and confess.

00:09:52.257 --> 00:09:54.693
Mukasey -- "In the heat
of a political campaign,

00:09:54.693 --> 00:09:57.262
on television, I'm
not saying Rudy necessarily,

00:09:57.262 --> 00:09:59.265
but everybody
embellishes everything."

00:09:59.265 --> 00:10:01.500
Giuliani -- "Oh,
you could throw a fake."

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:04.436
Mukasey -- "You're under no
obligation to tell the truth."

00:10:04.436 --> 00:10:06.872
Giuliani --
"You could throw a fake."

00:10:06.872 --> 00:10:08.273
What was the prep
for that meeting like?

00:10:08.273 --> 00:10:09.542
"Just keep your mouth shut,
Rudy,

00:10:09.542 --> 00:10:11.043
and I'll do the talking."
"Got it.

00:10:11.043 --> 00:10:13.278
I might jump in a few times
to say you can throw a fake."

00:10:13.278 --> 00:10:14.647
"Don't do that."
"I won't."

00:10:14.647 --> 00:10:17.016
"Maybe just a couple of times."
"Don't do it at all."

00:10:17.016 --> 00:10:19.484
"I'll just do it twice, but I'll
wait until they're recording."

00:10:19.484 --> 00:10:21.119
"Rudy!"
"I promise I won't do it."

00:10:21.119 --> 00:10:24.623
"Do you really promise?"
"No, I'm throwing a fake."

00:10:24.623 --> 00:10:27.126
The Republican Party is busy
trying to cement the big lie

00:10:27.126 --> 00:10:28.894
that the 2020 election
was stolen

00:10:28.894 --> 00:10:31.263
by using it to justify
new voter-suppression laws

00:10:31.263 --> 00:10:33.132
that will make it
both harder to vote

00:10:33.132 --> 00:10:35.234
and easier to overturn
results they don't like.

00:10:35.234 --> 00:10:37.536
Meanwhile, the people
who concocted that lie

00:10:37.536 --> 00:10:40.039
are facing major legal and
financial consequences

00:10:40.039 --> 00:10:43.041
because, in the court system,
facts still matter

00:10:43.041 --> 00:10:45.310
as opposed to
Republican politics, where...

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:46.845
-Nothing matters anymore.

00:10:46.845 --> 00:10:48.546
This has been "A Closer Look."

